#: 7744c1cc53f742de929d1e555c9e2549
msgid "The difference between a tutorial and how-to guide"
msgstr ""

#: d55c47cd75b341c0b0e3e897338fc37c
msgid ""
"In Diátaxis, tutorials and how-to guides are strongly distinguished. It’s a "
"distinction that’s often not made; in fact the single most common conflation"
" made in software product documentation is that between the *tutorial* and "
"the *how-to guide*."
msgstr ""

#: e1d9db4dd6e343d68d301ed4d4a5cadc
msgid ""
"So: what *is* the difference between tutorials and how to-guides? Why does "
"it matter? And why do they get confused?"
msgstr ""

#: 40ddb1f85c5443aa8a5464e06e588aed
msgid ""
"These are all good questions. Let’s start with the last one. *If the "
"distinction is really so important, why isn’t it more obvious?*"
msgstr ""

#: b02f7e22813349d996e661887324fcf3
msgid "What they have in common"
msgstr ""

#: 30fc1738af0f43cb9f2400786a487880
msgid ""
"In important respects, tutorials and how-to guides are indeed similar. They "
"are both practical guides: they contain directions for the user to follow. "
"They’re not there to explain or convey information. They exist to guide the "
"user in what to *do* rather than what there is *to know or understand*."
msgstr ""

#: 29d29825a44f4aac871e827fa0150db3
msgid ""
"They both set out steps for the reader to follow, and they both promise that"
" if the reader follows those steps, they’ll arrive at a successful "
"conclusion. Neither of them make much sense except for the user who has "
"their hands on the machinery, ready to do things. They both describe ordered"
" sequences of actions. You can’t expect success unless you perform the "
"actions in the right order."
msgstr ""

#: 532cf96268be43eb977562dfe0756928
msgid ""
"They are closely related, and like many close relations, can be mistaken for"
" one another at first glance."
msgstr ""

#: dca6ec2ac3264348a32c2a34fc57f72b
msgid "What matters is what the user needs"
msgstr ""

#: 699d833c1ecf43709389078384d7ff62
msgid ""
"Diátaxis insists that what matters in documentation is the needs of the "
"user, and it's by paying attention to this that we can correctly distinguish"
" between tutorials and how-to guides."
msgstr ""

#: 314bd0875bbe48d6b3dd0569218cc257
msgid ""
"Sometimes the user is **at study**, and sometimes the user is **at work**. "
"Documentation has to serve both those needs."
msgstr ""

#: 2a84edbd89e6460e8e41b3e0b443d9c9
msgid ""
"A tutorial serves the needs of the user who is at study. Its obligation is "
"*to provide a successful learning experience*. A how-to guide serves the "
"needs of the user who is at work. Its obligation is *to help the user "
"accomplish a task*. These are completely different needs and obligations, "
"and they are why the distinction between tutorials and how-to guides "
"matters: tutorials are **learning-oriented**, and how-to guides are **task-"
"oriented**."
msgstr ""

#: 7d8d10eecb17456a9f86d5372223a358
msgid "At study and at work"
msgstr ""

#: 343aa3371cde4ecc9be42450de1f155e
msgid ""
"We can consider this from the perspective of an actual example. Let’s say "
"you’re in medicine: a doctor, someone who needs to acquire and apply the "
"practical, clinical skills of their craft."
msgstr ""

#: 0502961d01aa4bf394aa56c8def91758
msgid ""
"As a doctor, sometimes you will be in work situations, *applying your "
"skills*, and sometimes you will be in study situations, *acquiring skills* "
"(all good doctors, even those with long careers behind them, continue to "
"study to improve their skills)."
msgstr ""

#: 9689594d8dbe49e69a7ea88b7024019f
msgid "At study"
msgstr ""

#: c8bea69d5d8244e5b10fb8735e0fc487
msgid ""
"Early on in your training, you’ll learn how to suture a wound. You’ll start "
"in the lab with your fellow students, at benches with small skin pads in "
"front of you (skin pads are blocks of synthetic material in various layers "
"that represent the epidermis, fat and other tissues. They have a similar "
"hardness and texture to human flesh, and behave somewhat similarly when "
"they’re cut and stitched). You’ll be provided with exactly what you need - "
"gloves, scalpel, needle, thread and so on - and step-by-step you’ll be shown"
" what to do, and what will happen when you do it."
msgstr ""

#: 65038b7d655444f18346cdf265dd479d
msgid ""
"And then it’s your turn. You will pick up the scalpel and tentatively draw "
"it across the top of the pad, and make an ineffectual incision into the top "
"layer (maybe a teaching assistant will tease you, asking what this poor pad "
"has done, that it deserves such a nasty scratch). Your neighbour will look "
"dismayed at their own attempt, a ragged cut of wildly uneven depths that "
"looks like something from a knife-fight."
msgstr ""

#: 6687d1988d3f442d969d62264755333a
msgid ""
"After a few attempts, with feedback and correction from the tutor, you’ll "
"have made a more or less clean cut that mostly goes through the fat layer "
"without cutting into the muscle beneath. Triumph!"
msgstr ""

#: 5ee932b40d0a44f6b756ac2246f3eadd
msgid ""
"But now you’re being asked to stitch it back up again! You’ll watch the "
"tutor demonstrate deftly and precisely, closing the wound in the pad with a "
"few neat, even stitches. You, on the other hand, will fumble with the "
"thread. You will hold things in the wrong hand and the wrong way round and "
"put them down in the wrong places. You will drop the needle. The thread will"
" fall out. You will be told off for failing to maintain sterility."
msgstr ""

#: c3d18b1c9c2a4ec9b31ba108289dcb07
msgid ""
"Eventually, you’ll actually get to stitch the wound. You will puncture the "
"skin in the wrong places and tear the edges of the cut. Your final result "
"will be an ugly scene of stretched and puckered skin and crude, untidy "
"stitches. The teaching assistants will have some critical things to say even"
" about parts of it that you thought you’d got right."
msgstr ""

#: 52e12c64e479438c97366f4a10077a64
msgid ""
"But, *you will have stitched your first wound*. And you will come back to "
"this lesson again and again, and bit by bit your fumbling will turn into "
"confident practice. You will have acquired basic competence. You will have "
"**learned by doing**."
msgstr ""

#: b2d45edcf36044219e09f00b3a7c6653
msgid ""
"This is a tutorial. It’s a *lesson*, safely in the hands of an instructor, a"
" teacher who looks after the interests of a pupil."
msgstr ""

#: 54a75c8855a0497382c8ff048f72b464
msgid "At work"
msgstr ""

#: 76d49edd8a3e43779307dea7301ee07e
msgid ""
"Now, let’s think about the doctor at work. As a doctor at work, you are "
"already competent. You have learned and refined clinical skills such as "
"suturing, as well as many others, and you’re able to put them together on a "
"daily basis to apply them to medical situations in the real world."
msgstr ""

#: 917bf822748d416e808d2cd7bc6a5dc6
msgid ""
"Consider a standard appendectomy. A clinical manual will list the equipment "
"and personnel required in the theatre. It will show how to station the "
"members of the team, and how to lay out the required tools, stands and "
"monitors. It will proceed step-by-step through the actions the team will "
"need to follow, ending with the formal handover to the post-operative team."
msgstr ""

#: 82fe371b16f743f5993598b8ffb87524
msgid ""
"The manual will show what incisions need to be made where, but they will "
"depend on whether you’re performing an open or a laparoscopic procedure, "
"whether you have pre-operative imaging to rely on or not, and so on. It will"
" include special steps or checks to be made in the case of an infant or "
"juvenile patient, or when converting to an open appendectomy mid-procedure. "
"Many of the steps will be of the form *if this, then that*."
msgstr ""

#: 0bbd58e7136045b7941c71d03ef5ae00
msgid ""
"Having a manual helps ensure that all the steps are done in the right order "
"and none are omitted. As a team, you’ll check through details of a procedure"
" to remind yourselves of key steps; sometimes you'll refer to it during the "
"procedure itself."
msgstr ""

#: 6209bb1ba6884f01bd94bdc3a400abaa
msgid ""
"Even for routine surgical operations, clinical manuals contain lists of "
"steps and checks. These manuals are how-to guides. They are not there to "
"teach you - you already have your skills. You already know these processes. "
"They are there to guide you safely in your clinical practice to accomplish a"
" particular task - **they serve your work**."
msgstr ""

#: 4989414987cf474ca179439b2f801b48
msgid "Understanding the distinction"
msgstr ""

#: 2bebeb351e7e45cf95c53a9125d5aff8
msgid ""
"The distinction between a lesson in medical school and a clinical manual is "
"the distinction between a tutorial and a how-to guide."
msgstr ""

#: 520eb787cbad427fb9c273975bcb350f
msgid ""
"A tutorial’s purpose is **to help the pupil acquire basic competence**."
msgstr ""

#: eba85b4644664c00822d3e29d04009a7
msgid ""
"A how-to guide’s purpose is **to help the already-competent user perform a "
"particular task correctly**."
msgstr ""

#: e21202da2e7749f496ff941703e65399
msgid ""
"A tutorial **provides a learning experience**. People learn skills through "
"practical, hands-on experience. What matters in a tutorial is what the "
"learner *does*, and what they experience while doing it."
msgstr ""

#: 9285e60009814225a24b52d778c6ad9d
msgid "A how-to guide **directs the user’s work**."
msgstr ""

#: e561fd9bdca94b0aaa98d5ba8e475b6f
msgid ""
"The tutorial follows a **carefully-managed path**, starting at a given point"
" and working to a conclusion. Along that path, the learner must have the "
"*encounters* that the lesson requires."
msgstr ""

#: 21e67af39ebd49e7aa1b24952fdf3384
msgid ""
"The how-to guide aims for a successful *result*, and guides the user along "
"the safest, surest way to the goal, but **the path can’t be managed**: it’s "
"the real world, and anything could appear to disrupt the journey."
msgstr ""

#: bca2037e51454292b378521cbb8d2b03
msgid ""
"A tutorial **familiarises the learner** with the work: with the tools, the "
"language, the processes and the way that what they’re working with behaves "
"and responds, and so on. Its job is to introduce them, manufacturing a "
"structured, repeatable encounter with them."
msgstr ""

#: 6b824546de064f519ccf96d3b8aa3c07
msgid "The how-to guide can and should **assume familiarity** with them all."
msgstr ""

#: f860f91320134701b2d84bd238805e34
msgid ""
"The tutorial takes place in a **contrived setting**, a learning environment "
"where as much as possible is set out in advance to ensure a successful "
"experience."
msgstr ""

#: fcbf237f63354a46bd80993dcdf20aff
msgid ""
"A how-to guide applies to the **real world**, where you have to deal with "
"what it throws at you."
msgstr ""

#: 071fe1fbfb934c8aa87add6da8fe759d
msgid "The tutorial **eliminates the unexpected**."
msgstr ""

#: e6b523dc58b647119042293ba1b1cd2a
msgid ""
"The how-to guide must **prepare for the unexpected**, alerting the user to "
"its possibility and providing guidance on how to deal with it."
msgstr ""

#: ebbf49ace96340faaf6d288db0c1b8d8
msgid ""
"A tutorial’s path follows a single line. **It doesn’t offer choices or "
"alternatives**."
msgstr ""

#: 5d6dd5c8492341688cd0defcf4025ee3
msgid ""
"A **how-to guide will typically fork and branch**, describing different "
"routes to the same destination: *If this, then that. In the case of ..., an "
"alternative approach is to…*"
msgstr ""

#: 9a78f15d26984dd2a0ef0c2bc4a0e70b
msgid ""
"A tutorial **must be safe**. No harm should come to the learner; it must "
"always be possible to go back to the beginning and start again."
msgstr ""

#: d42df34b4cf84d57bde6b68d12eeef02
msgid ""
"A how-to guide **cannot promise safety**; often there’s only one chance to "
"get it right."
msgstr ""

#: 2e3c3a6df9d44c6693be4a47c6143b5c
msgid ""
"In a tutorial, **responsibility lies with the teacher**. If the learner gets"
" into trouble, that's the teacher's problem to put right."
msgstr ""

#: 311b60eba5f145698c6559e5622570f7
msgid ""
"In a how-to guide, **the user has responsibility** for getting themselves in"
" and out of trouble."
msgstr ""

#: 6dff502c5d57467c8fde4a4fac17d309
msgid ""
"The learner **may not even have sufficient competence to ask the questions**"
" that a tutorial answers."
msgstr ""

#: f00a80de0f004d978be1a34a474cc101
msgid ""
"A how-to guide can assume that **the user is asking the right questions in "
"the first place**."
msgstr ""

#: 606d37f4d507483eafad20696ce2db46
msgid ""
"The tutorial is **explicit about basic things** - where to do things, where "
"to put them, how to manipulate objects. It addresses the embodied experience"
" - in our medical example, how hard to press, how to hold an implement; in a"
" software tutorial, it could be where to type a command, or how long to wait"
" for a response."
msgstr ""

#: 7cd0ccee075945ee8bd4f556ffb0848c
msgid ""
"A how-to guide relies on this as **implicit knowledge** - even bodily "
"knowledge."
msgstr ""

#: adf2221393eb401993cb2098b15fdcc1
msgid ""
"A tutorial is **concrete and particular** in its approach. It refers to the "
"specific, known, defined tools, materials, processes and conditions that we "
"have carefully set before the learner."
msgstr ""

#: 8ba5e8749d8842d69a07c1c1b9b4a774
msgid ""
"The how-to guide has to take a **general** approach: many of these things "
"will be unknowable in advance, or different in each real-world case."
msgstr ""

#: 9e75445613454f69800bdea4a7b42812
msgid ""
"The tutorial **teaches general skills and principles** that later could be "
"applied to a multitude of cases."
msgstr ""

#: 44ef882ce8514495af00097cb97aeeb6
msgid ""
"The user following a how-to guide is doing so in order to **complete a "
"particular task**."
msgstr ""

#: 8032250d64c24faf9c06a8cbdbfbdcf7
msgid ""
"None of these distinctions are arbitrary. They all emerge from the "
"distinction between **study** and **work**, which we understand as a key "
"distinction in making sense of what the user of documentation needs."
msgstr ""

#: 7687d053c9cf45b8b705d14440e5d997
msgid "The basic and the advanced"
msgstr ""

#: 12c64441622a4073bb4de15c031c3700
msgid ""
"A common but understandable conflation is to see the difference between "
"tutorials and how-to guides as being the difference between **the basic** "
"and **the advanced**."
msgstr ""

#: 83d17099886d420484eb0745669aa3ab
msgid ""
"After all, tutorials are for learners, while how-to guides are for already-"
"skilled practitioners. Tutorials must cover the basics, while how-to guides "
"have to deal with complexities that learners should not have to face."
msgstr ""

#: 34134457d6844f6998205f20b640e366
msgid ""
"However, there’s more to the story. Consider a clinical procedure manual: it"
" could be a manual for a basic routine procedure, of very low complexity. It"
" could describe steps for mundane matters such as correct completion of "
"paperwork or disposal of particular materials. *How-to guides can, do and "
"often should cover basic procedures.*"
msgstr ""

#: 0f240d515d584f9e9ddeaabd543b7550
msgid ""
"At the same time, even as a qualified doctor, you will find yourself back in"
" training situations. Some of them may be very advanced and specialised, "
"requiring a high level of skill and expertise already."
msgstr ""

#: ce09d890058b46ab914df0971864a5f5
msgid ""
"Let’s say you’re an anaesthetist of many years’ experience, who attends a "
"course: “Difficult neonatal intubations”. The practical part of the course "
"will be a learning experience: a lesson, safely in the hands of the "
"instructors, that will have you performing particular exercises to develop "
"your skills - just as it was when years earlier, you were learning to suture"
" your first wound."
msgstr ""

#: 57f960a92a284583b7fc7a6c4c3a4380
msgid ""
"The complexity is wholly different though, and so is the baseline of skills "
"required even to participate in the learning experience. But, it’s of the "
"same form, and serves the same kind of need, as that much earlier lesson."
msgstr ""

#: 8293fd2218ca41f491ee7ff56f21fda6
msgid ""
"It’s the same in software documentation: a tutorial can present something "
"complex or advanced. And, a how-to guide can cover something that’s basic or"
" well-known. The difference between the two lies in the need they serve: "
"**the user’s study**, or **their work**."
msgstr ""

#: 47cbe4c4663c45fa9474c2c163ebacfd
msgid "Safety and success"
msgstr ""

#: e43197a90fd4430f9c11bf027b03c869
msgid ""
"Understanding these distinctions, and the reason for upholding them, is "
"crucial to creating successful documentation. A clinical manual that "
"conflated education with practice, that tried to teach while at the same "
"time providing a guide to a real-world procedure would be a literally deadly"
" document. It would kill people."
msgstr ""

#: 75c06287307d4adfbaed6fe238f44843
msgid ""
"In disciplines such as software documentation, we get away with a great "
"deal, because our conflations and mistakes rarely kill anyone. However, we "
"can cause a great deal of low-level inconvenience and unhappiness to our "
"users, and we add to it, every single time we publish a tutorial or how-to "
"guide that doesn’t understand whether its purpose is to help the user in "
"their study - the acquisition of skills - or in their work - the application"
" of skills."
msgstr ""

#: a647a6af47ee4b9481d29c879e5d1711
msgid ""
"What’s more, we hurt ourselves too. Users don’t have to use our product. If "
"our documentation doesn’t bring them to success - if it doesn’t meet the "
"needs that they have at a particular stage in their cycle of interaction "
"with our product - they will find something else that does, if they can."
msgstr ""

#: d7cf2baf2d1f4661a19f7de1739c8b4a
msgid ""
"The conflation of tutorials and how-to guides is by no means the only one "
"made between different kinds of documentation, but it's one of the easiest "
"to make. It's also a particularly harmful one, because it risks getting in "
"the way of those newcomers whom we hope to turn into committed users. For "
"the sake of those users, and of our own product, getting the distinction "
"right is a key to success."
msgstr ""
